        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="2" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="0" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the infiltration test, we noticed some air leakage on the following:

- Windows: Living room, kitchen (over sink), bedrooms

- Both front and rear doors

- Attic hatch (Presence of ice around the attic hatch)

- Electric receptacles

- Combustion air supply

The results showed a medium level of air changing per hour. We recommend increasing the sealing of the building to lower the level of air changing.

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the time of the inspection, we noticed that the insulation level was estimated to be R-19. This insulation value is far under the actual standard of R-28. 

We recommend increasing the level of insulation to meet the actual standard.



</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>The access to the attic was impossible due to the presence of ice on the attic hatch frame. This is a sign of heat loss. Due to this situation we estimated the insulation level according to the tenant information. Therefore, we estimated the insulation to be R-40 (12??????????????????) of batt insulation. The attic insulation level is under the actual standard of R-60.

We recommend adding insulation to meet the standard.



</ceilings>
                <foundation>At the time of the audit, we noticed that the basement is not insulated. The concrete wall, when not properly insulated, cools down the house due to the thermal bridge transmitting cold by conduction. 

We also noticed air coming from the header joists.

We recommend the insulation of the foundation walls and the header joists.



</foundation>
                <windows>At the time of the audit, we noticed that the windows latches were broken, and the windows remained open and therefore, cooled down the house.</windows>
                <doors>At the time of the inspection, we noticed that the exterior doors are leaky around the doorknob and on the lower section.    </doors>
                <VentilationSystem> At the time of the inspection we noticed air leakage from the bathroom?????????s ventilation fans.</VentilationSystem>
                <AdditionalComments>We noticed a big difference of temperature between the basement and the rest of the house. The lack of insulation in the basement causes heat loss and arises the energy required to heat the building.</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
